Source: rustls-ffi
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
# cargo, rustc and cargo-c are not listed: this is built with the builder's own rustup toolchain (see build.sh),
# which dpkg's dependency check cannot see.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               pkgconf,
Standards-Version: 4.7.3
Homepage: https://github.com/rustls/rustls-ffi
Rules-Requires-Root: no

# The soname is librustls.so.<upstream version>: every release is its own soname, so the package is named after
# it. build.sh replaces @SOVER@ by the upstream version.
Package: librustls@SOVER@
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: C bindings for the Rustls TLS library
 rustls-ffi lets programs that are not written in Rust use Rustls, a TLS
 library written in Rust. curl can use it as a TLS backend (--with-rustls).
 .
 This build uses the aws-lc-rs crypto provider, which has the HPKE support
 that Encrypted Client Hello needs, and enables certificate compression
 (brotli and zlib).

Package: librustls-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: librustls@SOVER@ (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: C bindings for the Rustls TLS library (development files)
 rustls-ffi lets programs that are not written in Rust use Rustls, a TLS
 library written in Rust.
 .
 This package provides the header (rustls.h), the librustls.so link and the
 rustls.pc file for pkg-config. There is no static library: it is 40 MB and
 nothing here needs it.
